{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Why</b> — this is the violence that a violent man does. 'Violence' and 'trouble' are nouns that encompass every transgression and every sin that a man labors at, for it is violence and trouble and vain toil, and the word למה serves on account of another [word]." "<b>Why do You look at trouble</b> — the meaning is: how can a man do violence and trouble in the place of Your governance. And the meaning [of תביט] is 'lift, exalt,' or 'lift the head.' Yefet said: 'and he was a man of strife,' like 'and I am prayer' (1 Samuel 1:28 — reading איש ריב)."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:49.903258944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}